<%#
  CZID-285 — Layer 3 export-screening start page (the clearance hand-off for SIGNED-IN users).

  Approval model (legal-approved 2026-08-24): clearance is attestation + denied-party screening, with NO
  document identity-verification step. This page hands off to the screen; the POST runs it server-side and
  records the outcome (with the reference stub that is a PENDING clearance, i.e. deny, the correct dark-mode
  behavior).

  Dependency-free (no React/webpack entry): renders inside the SPA shell (blank navy header + white logo)
  but the content is plain ERB, so the gate works even if JS fails. Styling comes from the shared,
  brand-tokened partial (export_control/_styles).

  FORM CONTRACT (unchanged): a single POST to export_control_clearances_path with NO fields; the create
  action screens current_user server-side. Do not add inputs or rename the action.
%>
<%= render "export_control/styles" %>
<main class="ec-page">
  <div class="ec-card">
    <h1 class="ec-h1">
      Export-control screening required
    </h1>

    <div class="ec-panel">
      <p>
        Access to export-controlled data and functions on this service requires that you be screened against
        U.S. denied- and restricted-party lists. To proceed, your account will be screened before access is
        granted.
      </p>
    </div>

    <%= form_with url: export_control_clearances_path, method: :post, local: true do %>
      <%# The clearance version being recorded; surfaced here for the record. %>
      <p class="ec-meta">Clearance version: <%= @clearance_version %></p>

      <div class="ec-actions">
        <button type="submit" class="ec-btn ec-btn--primary">
          Continue
        </button>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</main>
